---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL;
---

<Base title="About | Jeremy Hoover" description="Jeremy Hoover builds product systems, design workflows, and AI-powered tools. He is an HCI MA student at Reichman University and an instructor at the UX Content Collective.">

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container container--narrow">

      <p class="eyebrow">About</p>
      <h1>Jeremy Hoover</h1>
      <p class="subtitle">Product strategy · Design systems · AI workflows</p>

      <div class="about-body">
        <p>
          I design customer-facing developer tools, content experiences, and product workflows, as
          well as internal systems that teams depend on. At Microsoft Fabric, my work spans content and product
          design for CI/CD, CLI, and MCP experiences. I also own the design automation repo our
          30-person design and PM team uses, a system I built from scratch that saw immediate adoption
          and now supports everything from daily prototyping to senior leadership demos.
        </p>
        <p>
          My background is unusual for someone doing this work. I started in journalism and history,
          moved into content and UX writing, and kept pushing further into the technical side until
          I was building agentic workflows, shipping skills to production, and contributing to
          open-source Microsoft tooling. I think that path is a feature: I bridge the human side
          of product problems with the technical side of building systems.
        </p>
        <p>
          On top of that, I've driven org-wide AI initiatives at Microsoft. I initiated a content
          design agent that was adopted and used by 150+ designers, and I was a key contributor to the
          Fabric CLI's AI assets layer, the part the Corporate VP of Product highlighted when
          it shipped GA. I'm also an instructor at the UX Content Collective, where I created
          the Technical Content Designer program, and I'm completing an MA in Human-Computer
          Interaction at Reichman University.
        </p>
        <p>
          I'm part of the Content Design Leaders Upstream group, led by Kate Agena, PhD,
          VP of Content Design at SAP. This keeps me connected to where the broader field
          is heading.
        </p>

        <hr class="divider" />

        <h2>Experience</h2>
        <div class="experience">
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Microsoft</strong>
              <span>February 2022 – Present</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">Senior Content Designer, AI systems and developer experiences</p>
            <p>
              Designing customer-facing content and product experiences for CI/CD, CLI, and MCP tools.
              Building AI-powered workflows and evaluation frameworks for developer and design tools.
              Owner of the team's AI design automation repo and a key contributor to org-wide AI initiatives.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>UX Content Collective</strong>
              <span>May 2026 – Present</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">Creator and instructor, Technical Content Designer Program</p>
            <p>Creator and instructor of the Technical Content Designer program, helping content designers build confidence with developer tools and AI systems.</p>
          </div>
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Wix.com</strong>
              <span>2018 – 2022</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">Senior UX Writer → Accessibility Champion</p>
            <p>
              Lead UX writer and editor for Wix Code. Led content strategy across products,
              coordinated localization for 15+ languages, ran usability testing, and contributed
              to the Words Matter blog. Accessibility champion across the org and hackathon winner.
            </p>
          </div>
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Natural Intelligence</strong>
              <span>2016 – 2018</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">Content Manager</p>
            <p>Managed, wrote, and edited content for multiple websites. Used Tableau to run content tests, analyze results, and drive data-informed content decisions.</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="divider" />

        <h2>Education</h2>
        <div class="experience">
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Reichman University</strong>
              <span>2026 – 2027</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">MA, Human-Computer Interaction · Merit scholarship recipient</p>
          </div>
          <div class="experience__item">
            <div class="experience__meta">
              <strong>Metropolitan State University of Denver</strong>
              <span>2006 – 2011</span>
            </div>
            <p class="experience__role">BA, History · Minor in Journalism · Helen Verba Award, Society of Professional Journalists</p>
          </div>
        </div>

        <hr class="divider" />

        <div class="cta-row">
          <a href={`${base}/#projects`} class="btn">See selected projects</a>
          <a href="mailto:jeremyd.hoover@gmail.com" class="btn btn--ghost">Get in touch</a>
        </div>
      </div>

    </div>
  </section>

</Base>

<style>
  .eyebrow {
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    letter-spacing: 0.08em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-4);
    max-width: none;
  }
  h1 { margin-bottom: var(--space-2); }
  .subtitle {
    font-size: var(--size-lg);
    color: var(--color-text-muted);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-12);
    max-width: none;
  }
  .about-body p {
    font-size: var(--size-lg);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-6);
  }
  h2 { margin-bottom: var(--space-8); }

  .experience { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: var(--space-8); }
  .experience__item {}
  .experience__meta {
    display: flex;
    justify-content: space-between;
    align-items: baseline;
    gap: var(--space-4);
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-1);
  }
  .experience__meta strong { font-size: var(--size-base); }
  .experience__meta span { font-size: var(--size-sm); color: var(--color-text-muted); }
  .experience__role {
    font-size: var(--size-base);
    font-weight: 500;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-2);
    max-width: none;
  }
  .experience__item p { font-size: var(--size-base); color: var(--color-text-muted); }

  .btn {
    display: inline-block;
    font-size: var(--size-sm);
    font-weight: 600;
    padding: 0.65rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: var(--radius-md);
    background: var(--color-accent);
    color: #fff;
    text-decoration: none;
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }
  .btn:hover { background: var(--color-accent-hover); color: #fff; }
  .btn--ghost {
    background: transparent;
    color: var(--color-accent);
    border: 1.5px solid var(--color-accent);
  }
  .btn--ghost:hover { background: var(--color-tag-bg); color: var(--color-accent-hover); }
  .cta-row { display: flex; gap: var(--space-4); flex-wrap: wrap; }
</style>
